<title>USA: Fidelity cuts 97 jobs from systems group - report.</title>
<headline>Fidelity cuts 97 jobs from systems group - report.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Investments cut 97 jobs from its systems group but will offer all the employees placements in other parts of the company, the Boston Herald reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Those workers who decide not to stay with Fidelity will be offered severance and placement help, the Herald said.</p>
<p>An additional 85 contract workers, not on Fidelity's permanent payroll, were also cut, according to the Herald.</p>
<p>The affected workers are part of two systems groups that Fidelity is merging into one unit, called Fidelity Security and Processing Group, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>((Boston bureau, (617) 367-4106))</p>
